% VERIFIED (READ) -- first page read 2026-09-22. J. Fluid Mech. (1985),
% vol. 161, pp. 217-237. DOI 10.1017/S0022112085002890.
% The experimental anchor for the acoustic section. From the abstract:
% a TRANSVERSE sound wave acting on a rigid circular cylinder IN A DUCT;
% "The frequency of vortex shedding can be shifted by sound applied either
% above or below the nominal vortex-shedding frequency. This entrainment is
% produced by the velocity induced by the sound wave rather than by the sound
% pressure." The introduction states that the resonant acoustic modes in such
% systems are transverse to both the mean flow and the cylinder axis, which
% is exactly the c_s/2H mode this project identifies.
% CAVEAT to state if cited: Re = 20 000 to 40 000, far above this project's
% range. Use hong2020lockin for the low-Re mechanism and this for the
% experimental precedent that sound entrains shedding at all.
